<h1>Blueberry-Lemon Cottage Cheese Pancakes</h1>

<p>
Soft, high-protein cottage cheese pancakes flavored with
fresh lemon and blueberries.
</p>

<p><strong>Servings:</strong> 1</p>

<div class="note">
<strong>Measurement rule:</strong>
Oats are weighed dry. Egg whites, whole egg and cottage cheese
are weighed before cooking.
</div>

<h2>Ingredients</h2>

<ul>
  <li>200 g Friendship 1% Low Fat No Salt Added Cottage Cheese</li>
  <li>150 g liquid egg whites</li>
  <li>50 g whole egg</li>
  <li>30 g dry old-fashioned oats</li>
  <li>75 g blueberries</li>
  <li>5 g lemon juice</li>
  <li>2 g lemon zest</li>
  <li>2 g vanilla extract</li>
  <li>2 g baking powder</li>
  <li>1 g cinnamon</li>
  <li>Cooking spray</li>
</ul>

<h2>Directions</h2>

<ol>
  <li>
    Add the cottage cheese, egg whites, whole egg, oats,
    lemon juice, lemon zest, vanilla, baking powder and
    cinnamon to a blender.
  </li>
  <li>Blend until smooth.</li>
  <li>Gently stir the blueberries into the batter.</li>
  <li>Coat a nonstick skillet with cooking spray.</li>
  <li>
    Cook pancakes over medium-low heat until the edges set
    and bubbles appear.
  </li>
  <li>Flip and cook the second side until done.</li>
  <li>Serve warm.</li>
</ol>

